From 53c28ffd12cb70ad0cc2b16bc9541bc279aba295 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Reichel <sebastian.reichel@collabora.com>
Date: Fri, 04 Sep 2026 18:17:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: vop2: Reset AXI during device bind

When VOP2 is already running due to a previous stage (e.g. vendor U-Boot
setups DSI display of the RK3588 EVB1), the system ends up with the
following error interrupt storm during boot:

rockchip-drm display-subsystem: [drm] *ERROR* POST_BUF_EMPTY irq err at vp3

The problem can be avoided by resetting VOP2 into a known state when
the device is being bound.

Signed-off-by: Sebastian Reichel <sebastian.reichel@collabora.com>

Link: https://gitlab.collabora.com/hardware-enablement/rockchip-3588/linux/-/commit/53c28ffd12cb70ad0cc2b16bc9541bc279aba295
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c
@@ -3014,6 +3014,8 @@ static int vop2_bind(struct device *dev, struct device *master, void *data)
 		return dev_err_probe(drm->dev, PTR_ERR(vop2->axi_rst),
 				     "failed to get axi reset\n");
 
+	vop2_reset_assert_deassert(vop2, vop2->axi_rst);
+
 	vop2->irq = platform_get_irq(pdev, 0);
 	if (vop2->irq < 0)
 		return dev_err_probe(drm->dev, vop2->irq, "cannot find irq for vop2\n");
